-- title:
--   Herbrand quotient of the S-units of a cyclic extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, and let $\sigma$ be an automorphism of $L$ over $K$ such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$; write $n = \#\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$. Let $S$ be a finite set of nonzero prime ideals of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and let $W$ be the set of nonzero primes $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ whose contraction to $\mathcal{O}_K$ lies in $S$, so that `W.unit L` is the group of $W$-units of $L$. Let $\Phi$ be a multiplicative automorphism of this unit group acting on underlying elements of $L$ by $\sigma$, and let $d$ and $N$ be endomorphisms of the additively written unit group determined on generators by $d(u) = \Phi(u) - u$ and $N(u) = \sum_{i=0}^{n-1} \Phi^i(u)$. Let $s_f(v)$ be the number of primes of $\mathcal{O}_L$ contracting to $v$, for $v$ a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and $s_i(v)$ the number of infinite places of $L$ restricting to $v$, for $v$ an infinite place of $K$. Then, with $t_0 = \#\bigl(\ker d / (\mathrm{im}\,N \cap \ker d)\bigr)$ and $t_1 = \#\bigl(\ker N / (\mathrm{im}\,d \cap \ker N)\bigr)$ (the intersections being taken inside the respective kernels, cardinalities as `Nat.card`),
--   $$t_0 \cdot n = \Bigl(\prod_{v \in S} n / s_f(v) \cdot \prod_{v \mid \infty} n / s_i(v)\Bigr) \cdot t_1,$$
--   the divisions being natural-number division and the second product ranging over all infinite places of $K$; moreover $t_0 \neq 0$.
--
--   This is the Herbrand-quotient computation for the $S$-units of a cyclic extension of number fields, in multiplicative form: $t_0$ and $t_1$ play the roles of the orders of $\hat H^0$ and $\hat H^{-1}$ of the cyclic group generated by $\sigma$ acting on the $W$-units, and $n/s_f(v)$, $n/s_i(v)$ are the local degrees at the places above $v$. It is the unit half of the Herbrand–Chevalley evaluation of the Herbrand quotient of the idèle class group, and is used for the idèle-class-group and adelic statements of that computation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_M4aHerbrand_sUnit_tateCard_mul_localDegreeProd.lean

